If you're using RH9 and want to play with a patched game, you might
find it more educational to roll your own binaries.  Here's a brief
how-to:

1) Download (to your home dir) the source tarball from
http://www.nethack.org/v342/download-src.html
2) Download (to your home dir) the hpmon and menucolors patches from
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html
3) Unpack the sources with tar xvzf nethack-342.tgz.  This will expand
into a directory called nethack-3.4.2/

Next, let's apply the source patches
4) cp *.diff nethack-3.4.2
5) patch -p1 < nethack-3.4.2/hpmon.diff
6) patch -p1 < nethack-3.4.2/nh342-menucolor.diff

(putting the diff files in nethack-3.4.2 and using -p1 makes sure the
name of the top level directory doesn't matter).

A little RH9 config changes:

7) go into the include directory, open config.h and find the lines
that look like:

/* path and file name extension for compression program */
 #define COMPRESS "/usr/bin/compress"  /* Lempel-Ziv compression */
 #define COMPRESS_EXTENSION ".Z"            /* compress's extension */
/* An example of one alternative you might want to use: */
/* #define COMPRESS "/usr/local/bin/gzip" */  /* FSF gzip compression
*/
/* #define COMPRESS_EXTENSION ".gz" */              /* normal gzip
extension */

Comment out the lines referring to /usr/bin/compress and uncomment the
lines referring to gzip.  Also, gzip is located at /bin/gzip in RH9.

Another useful change is to allow yourself to use wizard mode.  If so,
find the lines

#ifndef WIZARD          /* allow for compile-time or Makefile changes
*/
# ifndef KR1ED
#  define WIZARD  "wizard" /* the person allowed to use the -D option
*/
# else
#  define WIZARD
#  define WIZARD_NAME "wizard"
# endif
#endif

and replace "wizard" with "your_username" (whatever your_username
might be).

Finally you MUST include
#define HPMON
#define MENU_COLOR
somewhere in config.h.  Immediately below the WIZARD block is as good
a place as any.

Save config.h and exit.

8)  cd ../sys/unix
9)  sh setup.sh        This creates the makefiles

10) cd ../../src       You should be in ~/nethack-3.4.2/src now
11) Edit the Makefile and find the line

WINTTYLIB = -ltermlib
and comment it out (add # to the front of the line)

Remove the leading # from
#WINTTYLIB = -lncurses

Save and exit.  This will set up the game to use ASCII mode with the
ncurses library (IIRC, ncurses comes with Linux by default).

12) cd ..
13) make all
14) make install       Can be done as root, or prefixed with sudo

Optionally, make the documentation:

15)  cd doc
16)  make manpages      Again, do as root or use sudo
17)  make distrib       (Although I think make all covers this)

18)  Finally, you need to edit/create a .nethackrc file in your home
directory containing something like:

OPTIONS=menucolors
MENUCOLOR=" blessed "=cyan
MENUCOLOR=" holy "=cyan
MENUCOLOR=" cursed "=red
MENUCOLOR=" unholy "=red
MENUCOLOR=" cursed .* (being worn)"=red&underline

for the menu colors to actually work.

